	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataGovernanceGuidelinesBusinessObject">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Data Governance Guidelines]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataGovernanceGuidelinesBusinessObject</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Data Governance Guidelines]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: Data Governance Guidelines can be defined as a set of principles, rules, and practices that provide direction and guidance for managing and controlling data assets within an organization. These guidelines outline the framework for ensuring data quality, integrity, privacy, security, and compliance throughout the data lifecycle, including data collection, storage, usage, and sharing.

Source: Data Governance Institute

Source reference: https://datagovernance.com/goals-and-principles-for-data-governance/

LOST view: SV-Governance Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataGovernanceGuidelinesBusinessObject

