	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataQualityFrameworkBusinessObject">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Data Quality Framework]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataQualityFrameworkBusinessObject</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Data Quality Framework]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: A Data Quality Framework refers to a structured approach or set of guidelines that organizations use to assess, measure, and improve the quality of their data. It provides a systematic framework for managing data quality throughout its lifecycle, from data collection to data analysis and decision-making.

Source: European Commission

LOST view: SV-Governance Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataQualityFrameworkBusinessObject

