		<dcterms:description>The OpenAPI is a specification for building APIs (Application Programming Interfaces) that allows for a standard, language-agnostic interface to RESTful APIs. It is used to design, build, document, and consume REST APIs, enabling interoperability between different systems. The OpenAPI specification, formerly known as the Swagger specification, is developed by the OpenAPI Initiative, which includes more than 30 organizations from different areas of the tech industry.</dcterms:description>
