		<dcterms:description>Turtle (Terse RDF Triple Language) is a human-readable serialization format for representing RDF (Resource Description Framework) data. It provides a concise and compact syntax to express triples, which consist of subject-predicate-object statements. Turtle is widely used for creating and sharing RDF data due to its simplicity and readability.</dcterms:description>
