	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDF-XMLRepresentation">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[RDF-XML]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDF-XMLRepresentation</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[RDF-XML]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: RDF-XML (Resource Description Framework XML) is a syntax format used to represent metadata and structured data in the form of Resource Description Framework (RDF) triples. RDF-XML provides a way to encode and exchange data using XML (eXtensible Markup Language) syntax.

Publisher: W3C

Source: https://www.w3.org/TR/rdf-syntax-grammar/

LOST view: SV-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDF-XMLRepresentation

