	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonDataModelRepresentation">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Common Data Model]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonDataModelRepresentation</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Common Data Model]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: CDM is an ontology based on the FRBR model (Functional Requirements for Bibliographic Records). CDM uses  RDF(S)/OWL technologies, capable of representing relationships between the resource types managed by the Publications Office and their views. All within the scope of the FRBR model and, therefore, in terms of Work, Expression, Manifestation and Item.

Publisher: The Publications Office of the European Union

Source: https://op.europa.eu/en/web/eu-vocabularies/cdm

LOST view: SV-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonDataModelRepresentation

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonDataModelRepresentation

Interoperability Layer: Semantic

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataRepresentation

]]></skos:definition>
