		<skos:example><![CDATA[The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Fishcoin Project, is a project using Blockchain technologies for seafood traceability. https://fishcoin.co/]]></skos:example>
		<eira:iopSaliency><![CDATA[The Blockchain Application Component ABB is salient for interoperability because it implements a set of elements needed and used by blockchain services. Those aspects are peer network, smart contracts, membership, events, ledger, system integration, wallet, and system management. All listed components can be part of a digital public service enhancing trustability and enabling interoperability in a secure and reliable way.]]></eira:iopSaliency>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[In the creation of the Blockchain component, several actors such as developer, user, architect, regulator, operator, membership services, etc. are present in a blockchain that provides a solution to a blockchain-based business network. Each actor and component present in a blockchain plays a major role to make the network more secure and reliable.]]></skos:note>
