	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/Geo-LocalizationApplicationInterface">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Geo-Localization]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/Geo-LocalizationApplicationInterface</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Geo-Localization]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: The Geo-localization Application Service is a web service that provides functionality for determining and retrieving the geographic location of a device, user, or point of interest using various data sources and techniques. It enables applications to integrate location-based features and services, such as mapping, routing, proximity search, and geofencing, into their functionality. The Geo-localization Application Service utilizes a combination of technologies, including GPS, IP geolocation, Wi-Fi positioning, cellular network data, and geospatial algorithms, to accurately determine and track the location information. It offers a standardized and accessible interface for developers to query and utilize location data in their applications, allowing for enhanced user experiences, targeted services, and location-aware functionality

Source: European Location Framework (ELF)

Source reference: https://www.elfproject.eu/

LOST view: TVA-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/Geo-LocalizationApplicationInterface

ABB name: egovera:Geo-LocalizationApplicationInterface

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-11-20

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/Geo-LocalizationApplicationInterface

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Specialises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/WebServiceApplicationInterface

]]></skos:definition>
