		<skos:definition><![CDATA[The Geo-localization Application Service is a web service that provides functionality for determining and retrieving the geographic location of a device, user, or point of interest using various data sources and techniques. It enables applications to integrate location-based features and services, such as mapping, routing, proximity search, and geofencing, into their functionality. The Geo-localization Application Service utilizes a combination of technologies, including GPS, IP geolocation, Wi-Fi positioning, cellular network data, and geospatial algorithms, to accurately determine and track the location information. It offers a standardized and accessible interface for developers to query and utilize location data in their applications, allowing for enhanced user experiences, targeted services, and location-aware functionality]]></skos:definition>
