		<skos:note><![CDATA[It is based on the Eclipse Dataspace Connector (EDC) specification, which is an open standard for connecting data spaces. It is designed to be interoperable with other EDC-compliant connectors, allowing for the secure and federated sharing of data across different data spaces.It is implemented in Java and can be deployed on a variety of platforms, including on-premises servers, cloud platforms, and edge devices. It is available as a free and open source software project. The Intel IONOS Orbiter Connector is a valuable tool for organizations that need to share data securely and efficiently across different data spaces. It is easy to use and deploy, and it is compatible with a wide range of platforms.]]></skos:note>
