		<eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EFilesManagementApplicationService</eira:PURI>
		<dcterms:modified>2023-11-20</dcterms:modified>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EFilesManagementApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<dcterms:title><![CDATA[EFiles Management Application Service]]></dcterms:title>
		<dcterms:type>egovera:EFilesManagementApplicationService</dcterms:type>
		<skos:definition><![CDATA[An eFiles Management Digital Service is an electronic system designed to store, manage, and track electronic documents and other media files. It enables users to create, share, organize, and find documents in a centralized digital environment, often providing tools for version control, access permissions, and collaboration.]]></skos:definition>
		<eira:definitionSource><![CDATA[Techopedia]]></eira:definitionSource>
		<eira:definitionSourceReference><![CDATA[https://www.techopedia.com/definition/23759/electronic-file-management-system]]></eira:definitionSourceReference>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[Human Resources Document Management
An HR department uses an eFiles Management Digital Service to securely store employee records, including contracts, performance reviews, and personal information. The system allows HR staff to quickly retrieve documents for reference or auditing purposes and ensures that sensitive information is protected with appropriate access controls.

Legal Case File Organization
A law firm implements an eFiles Management Digital Service to manage case files. The system allows lawyers to access case-related documents from anywhere, collaborate on documents with version control, and ensure that all changes are tracked for legal compliance and accountability.

Educational Content Repository
A university uses an eFiles Management Digital Service to manage a repository of educational materials, including lecture notes, research papers, and multimedia content. Professors and students can access and contribute to the repository, which is organized by course and subject matter for ease of use.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[The eFiles Management Digital Service is a comprehensive solution that helps organizations transition from paper-based file management systems to digital ones. It encompasses a range of functionalities including document scanning and digitization, metadata tagging for easy search and retrieval, secure access controls to ensure data privacy and compliance with regulations, and audit trails for tracking document history. The service often integrates with other enterprise applications such as email, customer relationship management (CRM) systems, and enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems to streamline workflows and improve productivity. Additionally, it may offer features like automated workflows, electronic signatures, and mobile access to facilitate remote work and collaboration among team members.]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:eifLayer>TechnicalApplication</eira:eifLayer>
		<skos:broader>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService</skos:broader>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PrivacyApplicationService">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Privacy]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PrivacyApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Privacy]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: Privacy ABB is an Application Service enabling the share of functionalities such as storing, securing, anonymising, pseudonymising, rectifying and erasing personal data.

Source: ePrivacy Regulation

Source reference: https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/policies/eprivacy-regulation

Example: The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): SOLVIT - Solvit is a mailbox service for the access, rectification or deletion of personal data.(http://ec.europa.eu/solvit/privacy-statement/#maincontentSec8)

Interoperability Dimension: Structural IoP

LOST view: Technical view - application

Viewpoint: Interoperability Privacy viewpoint

Interoperability Saliency: The Privacy Service ABB  is salient for interoperability because "security and privacy are primary concerns in the provision of public services" (EIF) and, as stated in EIF Recommendation 15: "Define a common security and privacy framework and establish processes for public services to ensure secure and trustworthy data exchange between public administrations and in interactions with citizens and businesses."

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PrivacyApplicationService

ABB name: eira:PrivacyApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/PrivacyApplicationService

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

]]></skos:definition>
