		<skos:definition><![CDATA[Data encryption is the process of converting plain text or data into a coded form known as ciphertext, to prevent unauthorized access during transmission or storage. It uses cryptographic algorithms and keys to transform the data into an unreadable format, which can only be decrypted using the corresponding decryption key.]]></skos:definition>
