	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HashiCorpVaultApplicationService">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[HashiCorp Vault]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HashiCorpVaultApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[HashiCorp Vault]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: Vault is an open-source tool designed for securely storing and accessing sensitive information such as passwords, API keys, and encryption keys. It provides a centralized system for managing secrets and ensures their secure distribution across applications and systems.

Additional information: Vault offers a secure and scalable solution for managing secrets in modern IT environments. It employs a client-server architecture where the Vault server acts as a central repository for secrets, while clients interact with the server to retrieve or store secrets. Vault provides various authentication methods, access control policies, and encryption mechanisms to ensure the confidentiality and integrity of stored secrets. It also supports dynamic secrets, which are short-lived credentials generated on-demand, further enhancing security. Vault integrates with popular cloud platforms and can be seamlessly integrated into existing infrastructure.

Example: An example of Vault's application is in a microservices architecture where multiple services require access to sensitive information. Instead of hardcoding credentials within each service, Vault can be used to securely store and distribute these secrets. Services can authenticate with Vault and retrieve the required secrets dynamically, reducing the risk of exposure and simplifying secret management across the system.

Publisher: HashiCorp

Source: https://www.vaultproject.io/

LOST view: TVA-Privacy Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HashiCorpVaultApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HashiCorpVaultApplicationService

Name: Vault Application Service

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService

]]></skos:definition>
		<egovera:HashiCorpVaultApplicationService_Properties />
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HashiCorpVaultApplicationService_Properties">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Properties of HashiCorp Vault]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HashiCorpVaultApplicationService_Properties</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Properties of HashiCorp Vault]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HashiCorpVaultApplicationService" />
		<eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HashiCorpVaultApplicationService</eira:PURI>
		<dcterms:modified>2024-01-28</dcterms:modified>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HashiCorpVaultApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<dcterms:title><![CDATA[Vault Application Service]]></dcterms:title>
		<dcterms:description>Vault is an open-source tool designed for securely storing and accessing sensitive information such as passwords, API keys, and encryption keys. It provides a centralized system for managing secrets and ensures their secure distribution across applications and systems.</dcterms:description>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[An example of Vault's application is in a microservices architecture where multiple services require access to sensitive information. Instead of hardcoding credentials within each service, Vault can be used to securely store and distribute these secrets. Services can authenticate with Vault and retrieve the required secrets dynamically, reducing the risk of exposure and simplifying secret management across the system.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[Vault offers a secure and scalable solution for managing secrets in modern IT environments. It employs a client-server architecture where the Vault server acts as a central repository for secrets, while clients interact with the server to retrieve or store secrets. Vault provides various authentication methods, access control policies, and encryption mechanisms to ensure the confidentiality and integrity of stored secrets. It also supports dynamic secrets, which are short-lived credentials generated on-demand, further enhancing security. Vault integrates with popular cloud platforms and can be seamlessly integrated into existing infrastructure.]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:SolutionBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<dcterms:publisher><![CDATA[HashiCorp]]></dcterms:publisher>
		<dcterms:source><![CDATA[https://www.vaultproject.io/]]></dcterms:source>
		<eira:view>TVA-Privacy Enablers [Motivation]</eira:view>
		<eira:eifLayer>TechnicalApplication</eira:eifLayer>
		<eira:implementedBy>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService</eira:implementedBy>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataGovernanceApplicationService">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Data Governance (copy)]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataGovernanceApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Data Governance (copy)]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: Data Governance is the overall management of the availability, usability, integrity, and security of data within an organization. It encompasses the people, processes, and technologies required to ensure that data is properly managed throughout its lifecycle, from creation or acquisition to deletion or archival.

Source: Techopedia

Source reference: https://www.techopedia.com/definition/12797/data-governance

Additional information: Data Governance involves establishing and enforcing policies, procedures, and standards to ensure that data is accurate, consistent, and reliable. It aims to provide a framework for decision-making, accountability, and responsibility related to data management. This concept ensures that data is treated as a valuable asset and is used effectively to support business objectives, regulatory compliance, and data privacy requirements. Data Governance also involves defining roles and responsibilities, implementing data quality controls, and establishing data stewardship practices.

Example: An example of Data Governance in action is when an organization implements a data governance framework to ensure that all employees follow standardized data entry procedures, adhere to data classification policies, and comply with data protection regulations. This framework may include data governance committees, data stewards, data quality assessments, and data access controls to ensure that data is managed consistently and securely across the organization.

LOST view: TVA-Data Management Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataGovernanceApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:DataGovernanceApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-11-20

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataGovernanceApplicationService

Name: Data Governance Application Service

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Specialises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService

]]></skos:definition>
