		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/QuartzSchedulerApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<dcterms:title><![CDATA[Quartz Scheduler Application Service]]></dcterms:title>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[An example application of Quartz Scheduler is when sending einvoices on batches. Administrator can configure a cron expression for transferring einvoices to Central VIES once a day. If the solution is deployed using kubernetes, quartz will be not necessary since the developer/architect can take advantaga of the Kubernetes Scheduled Jobs.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:SolutionBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<dcterms:description>Quartz is an open source job-scheduling framework written entirely in Java and designed for use in both J2SE and J2EE applications. It offers great flexibility without sacrificing simplicity. You can create complex schedules for executing any job. Examples are e.g. tasks that run daily, every other Friday at 7:30 p.m. or only on the last day of every month.</dcterms:description>
		<dcterms:publisher><![CDATA[Software AG]]></dcterms:publisher>
		<dcterms:source><![CDATA[https://www.quartz-scheduler.org/]]></dcterms:source>
		<eira:view>TVI-Member State Deployment Model</eira:view>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CRMApplicationService">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[CRM]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CRMApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[CRM]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: CRM (Customer Relationship Management) as a web service refers to a set of APIs (Application Programming Interfaces) that enable the integration and utilization of CRM functionality within external applications or systems. It provides developers with the means to access and interact with CRM capabilities, such as customer data retrieval, data update, customer interaction tracking, and more. By exposing CRM functionality as a web service, organizations can achieve seamless interoperability and enhance customer engagement by integrating CRM features into various channels, platforms, and services.

Source: IEEE Xplore

LOST view: TVA-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CRMApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:CRMApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-11-20

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CRMApplicationService

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Specialises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataManagementApplicationService

]]></skos:definition>
