	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ApacheNiFiApplicationService">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Apache NiFi]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ApacheNiFiApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Apache NiFi]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: Apache NiFi is an open-source data integration and data flow automation tool that provides a visual interface to easily manage and control the movement of data between different systems. It allows users to design, build, and execute data flows, known as data pipelines, using a web-based graphical user interface (GUI). NiFi supports a wide range of data sources, destinations, and processors, enabling efficient data ingestion, transformation, routing, and monitoring.

Additional information: Apache NiFi is designed to handle real-time data streaming and batch processing, making it suitable for use cases such as IoT data collection, log aggregation, data migration, and data transformation. It provides a scalable and reliable platform for managing data flows across various systems, including databases, cloud storage, messaging systems, and more. NiFi's GUI allows users to visually create and modify data pipelines, making it accessible to both technical and non-technical users. It offers features like data provenance, security, data lineage, and extensive monitoring capabilities. NiFi also supports data governance and compliance requirements through features like data encryption, access control, and auditing.

Example: An example application of Apache NiFi is in a data lake architecture. NiFi can be used to ingest data from various sources like sensors, social media feeds, and databases into a centralized data lake. It can then perform data transformations, filtering, and enrichment before storing the processed data in a suitable format for downstream analytics. NiFi's visual interface makes it easy to design and manage complex data flows, ensuring efficient and reliable data movement within the data lake ecosystem.

Publisher: Apache NiFi - Official Website

Source: https://nifi.apache.org/

LOST view: TVA-Data Management Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ApacheNiFiApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ApacheNiFiApplicationService

Name: Apache NiFi Application Service

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService

]]></skos:definition>
		<egovera:ApacheNiFiApplicationService_Properties />
	</skos:Concept>
