	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ContainersOrchestratorApplicationService_Properties">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Properties of Containers Orchestrator]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ContainersOrchestratorApplicationService_Properties</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Properties of Containers Orchestrator]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ContainersOrchestratorApplicationService" />
		<eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ContainersOrchestratorApplicationService</eira:PURI>
		<dcterms:modified>2023-11-20</dcterms:modified>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ContainersOrchestratorApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<dcterms:title><![CDATA[Containers Orchestrator Application Service]]></dcterms:title>
		<dcterms:type>egovera:ContainersOrchestratorApplicationService</dcterms:type>
		<skos:definition><![CDATA[Containers Orchestrator is a software tool or platform that automates the deployment, management, and scaling of containerized applications. It provides a centralized control plane to efficiently manage and coordinate the deployment and operation of containers across a cluster of machines or nodes.]]></skos:definition>
		<eira:definitionSource><![CDATA[Wikipedia]]></eira:definitionSource>
		<eira:definitionSourceReference><![CDATA[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Container_orchestration]]></eira:definitionSourceReference>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[One popular example of a Containers Orchestrator is Kubernetes. It provides a robust and scalable platform for managing containerized applications. With Kubernetes, developers can define the desired state of their application using declarative configuration files, and the orchestrator takes care of deploying and managing the containers accordingly. It offers features like automatic scaling, rolling updates, service discovery, and load balancing, making it easier to deploy and manage applications in a distributed environment.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[Containers Orchestrator simplifies the management of containerized applications by abstracting away the underlying infrastructure complexities. It enables efficient resource utilization, load balancing, high availability, and fault tolerance. The orchestrator handles tasks such as container scheduling, service discovery, networking, storage management, and health monitoring. It allows developers to focus on application development and deployment, while ensuring scalability, resilience, and ease of management.]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:view>TVA-Containerization Enablers [Motivation]</eira:view>
		<eira:view>Technical view - application</eira:view>
		<eira:eifLayer>TechnicalApplication</eira:eifLayer>
		<skos:broader>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService</skos:broader>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TrustedDigitalRepositoriesApplicationService">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Trusted Digital Repositories]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TrustedDigitalRepositoriesApplicationService</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Trusted Digital Repositories]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: Trusted Digital Repositories refer to specialized eArchiving application services that are designed to preserve and provide long-term access to digital objects, such as documents, datasets, multimedia files, and other forms of digital content. These repositories follow established standards, best practices, and guidelines to ensure the integrity, authenticity, and usability of the archived materials over time. They employ robust storage, metadata management, and preservation strategies to safeguard the long-term viability and accessibility of digital assets. Trusted Digital Repositories play a crucial role in the preservation and curation of digital heritage, research data, and other valuable digital resources.

Source: ISO

LOST view: TVA-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TrustedDigitalRepositoriesApplicationService

