		<skos:note><![CDATA[Apache Atlas allows organizations to create a centralized repository of metadata that describes their data assets, such as databases, tables, columns, and relationships between them. It supports a wide range of data platforms and technologies, including Hadoop, relational databases, cloud storage, and more. With Apache Atlas, organizations can define and enforce data governance policies, such as data classification, access controls, and data lineage. It provides a comprehensive set of features for data discovery, data lineage tracking, data quality monitoring, and metadata search. Apache Atlas also integrates with other data management and governance tools, enabling seamless interoperability in the data ecosystem.]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:SolutionBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<dcterms:description>Apache Atlas is an open-source metadata management and governance framework for enterprises. It provides a scalable platform to capture, manage, and govern metadata about data assets across various systems in an organization. By enabling metadata management, Apache Atlas helps organizations gain insights into their data assets, ensure data quality, and enforce data governance policies.</dcterms:description>
