		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[FIWARE TRUE Connector]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: The FIWARE TRUE Connector is a software module that facilitates the exchange of data between FIWARE and the International Data Space (IDS) ecosystem. It provides a secure and reliable way to share data between different organizations, while ensuring that the data remains compliant with IDS standards.

Additional information: The FIWARE TRUE Connector is a key enabler for the IDS ecosystem, as it allows organizations to share data in a secure and compliant way. It is currently used by a number of organizations, including the European Commission and the City of Barcelona.

Example: The FIWARE TRUE Connector can be used to share data between different smart city applications. For example, it could be used to share data about traffic congestion between a traffic management system and a public transport app.

Publisher: FIWARE Foundation

Source: https://fiware-true-connector.readthedocs.io/en/latest/

LOST view: TVA-Data Space Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/FIWARETRUEConnectorApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/FIWARETRUEConnectorApplicationService

Name: FIWARE TRUE Connector Application Service

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService

]]></skos:definition>
