	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[RDF Mapping Language (RML)]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[RDF Mapping Language (RML)]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: This document describes RML, a generic mapping language, based on and extending [R2RML]. The RDF Mapping language (RML) is a mapping language defined to express customized mapping rules from heterogeneous data structures and serializations to the RDF [RDF-CONCEPTS] data model. RML is defined as a superset of the W3C-standardized mapping language [R2RML], aiming to extend its applicability and broaden its scope, adding support for data in other structured formats. [R2RML] is the W3C standard to express customized mappings from relational databases to RDF. RML follows exactly the same syntax as R2RML; therefore, RML mappings are themselves RDF graphs. The present document describes the RML language and its concepts through definitions and examples.

Interoperability Dimension: Structural IoP

Publisher: IDLab Ghent University

Source: https://rml.io/specs/rml/

LOST view: SV-Data Mapping

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject

Interoperability Layer: Semantic

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataMappingDataObject

]]></skos:definition>
		<egovera:RDFMappingLanguageDataObject_Properties />
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject_Properties">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Properties of RDF Mapping Language (RML)]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject_Properties</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Properties of RDF Mapping Language (RML)]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject" />
		<dcterms:modified>2024-01-28</dcterms:modified>
		<dcterms:publisher><![CDATA[IDLab Ghent University]]></dcterms:publisher>
		<dcterms:description>This document describes RML, a generic mapping language, based on and extending [R2RML]. The RDF Mapping language (RML) is a mapping language defined to express customized mapping rules from heterogeneous data structures and serializations to the RDF [RDF-CONCEPTS] data model. RML is defined as a superset of the W3C-standardized mapping language [R2RML], aiming to extend its applicability and broaden its scope, adding support for data in other structured formats. [R2RML] is the W3C standard to express customized mappings from relational databases to RDF. RML follows exactly the same syntax as R2RML; therefore, RML mappings are themselves RDF graphs. The present document describes the RML language and its concepts through definitions and examples.</dcterms:description>
		<dcterms:source><![CDATA[https://rml.io/specs/rml/]]></dcterms:source>
		<eira:concept>eira:SolutionBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject</eira:PURI>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject</dcterms:identifier>
		<eira:view>SV-Data Mapping</eira:view>
		<eira:view>SV-Functional Architecture Principles</eira:view>
		<eira:view>Semantic view - Motivation</eira:view>
		<eira:view>Semantic view</eira:view>
		<eira:eifLayer>Semantic</eira:eifLayer>
		<eira:implementedBy>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataMappingDataObject</eira:implementedBy>
		<eira:iopDimension>Structural IoP</eira:iopDimension>
	</skos:Concept>
