	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[ESPD-EDM]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[ESPD-EDM]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: The European Single Procurement Document (ESPD) is a standardized form used in public procurement processes within the European Union (EU). As a data object, the ESPD represents a structured document that contains essential information about a supplier or contractor. It includes details such as the company's identification, financial standing, technical and professional abilities, and any legal grounds for exclusion. The ESPD serves as a preliminary self-declaration by suppliers, allowing them to demonstrate their eligibility and suitability to participate in public procurement procedures across EU member states.

Interoperability Dimension: Structural IoP

Publisher: The Publications Office of the European Union

Source: https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/index.html

LOST view: SV-Business Agnostic Data Models

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject

Interoperability Layer: Semantic

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataModelDataObject

]]></skos:definition>
		<egovera:ESPD-EDMDataObject_Properties />
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject_Properties">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Properties of ESPD-EDM]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject_Properties</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Properties of ESPD-EDM]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject" />
		<dcterms:modified>2024-01-28</dcterms:modified>
		<dcterms:publisher><![CDATA[The Publications Office of the European Union]]></dcterms:publisher>
		<dcterms:description>The European Single Procurement Document (ESPD) is a standardized form used in public procurement processes within the European Union (EU). As a data object, the ESPD represents a structured document that contains essential information about a supplier or contractor. It includes details such as the company's identification, financial standing, technical and professional abilities, and any legal grounds for exclusion. The ESPD serves as a preliminary self-declaration by suppliers, allowing them to demonstrate their eligibility and suitability to participate in public procurement procedures across EU member states.</dcterms:description>
		<dcterms:source><![CDATA[https://docs.ted.europa.eu/ESPD-EDM/latest/index.html]]></dcterms:source>
		<eira:concept>eira:SolutionBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject</eira:PURI>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ESPD-EDMDataObject</dcterms:identifier>
