	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ODRLDataObject">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[ODRL]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ODRLDataObject</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[ODRL]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: The Organization Ontology is a standardized representation of organizational structures, roles, and relationships within the field of Linked Data and the Semantic Web. It provides a framework for describing and modeling various aspects of organizations, such as their hierarchy, departments, employees, and roles.

Publisher: W3C

Source: https://www.w3.org/TR/vocab-org/

LOST view: Semantic view

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ODRLDataObject

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ODRLDataObject

Interoperability Layer: Semantic

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Ontology

]]></skos:definition>
