	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/W3CShapesConstraintLanguageDataObject">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[W3C Shapes Constraint Language]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/W3CShapesConstraintLanguageDataObject</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[W3C Shapes Constraint Language]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: The Shapes Constraint Language (SHACL) is a language and framework for describing and validating the structure and constraints of RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs. RDF is a standard for representing data in a graph format, widely used in the Semantic Web.

Interoperability Dimension: Structural IoP

Publisher: W3C

Source: https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/

LOST view: SV-Agnostic Ontologies

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/W3CShapesConstraintLanguageDataObject

