		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/GoldenRecordDataObject" />
		<eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/GoldenRecordDataObject</eira:PURI>
		<dcterms:modified>2023-11-20</dcterms:modified>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/GoldenRecordDataObject</dcterms:identifier>
		<dcterms:type>egovera:GoldenRecordDataObject</dcterms:type>
		<dcterms:title><![CDATA[Golden Record]]></dcterms:title>
		<eira:definitionSource><![CDATA[Eurpean Comission Data Management]]></eira:definitionSource>
		<eira:definitionSourceReference><![CDATA[https://ec.europa.eu/research/participants/docs/h2020-funding-guide/cross-cutting-issues/open-access-data-management/open-access_en.htm]]></eira:definitionSourceReference>
		<skos:definition><![CDATA["Golden Record" refers to a single, authoritative, and complete version of a data entity or a set of data that serves as the reference source for all other copies or instances of that data]]></skos:definition>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): EU-ERS: Master Data Register. https://circabc.europa.eu/ui/group/3cc8c417-0f2a-4eb4-8ff7-10d60638446a/information]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[In the context of data management, a Golden Record is the definitive copy of a data entity which may include customer profiles, product information, or any other type of organizational data. This record is created by integrating, cleansing, and consolidating data from various sources to ensure that it is the most reliable source of truth. The Golden Record is essential in scenarios where consistent data quality is critical, such as in customer relationship management (CRM), enterprise resource planning (ERP), or master data management (MDM) systems. It is used to provide a consistent and accurate view of data across different business units and applications, thereby reducing errors, improving decision-making, and enhancing operational efficiency.]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:eifLayer>Semantic</eira:eifLayer>
		<skos:broader>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataSetCatalogueDataObject</skos:broader>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/APICatalogueDataObject">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[API Catalogue]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/APICatalogueDataObject</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[API Catalogue]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: API Catalogue ABB is a Data Object that corresponds to a collection of (open) software interfaces that allow data consumption by a specific digital solution

Source: Inspired in JRC

Source reference: https://data.jrc.ec.europa.eu/dataset/5a431f38-1e2c-449a-898e-34f2a3234c3b

Example: The following implementation is an example on how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): RapidAPI - RapidAPI is a collection of predefined APIs that are free to test, specifically updated for 2021. https://rapidapi.com/collection/list-of-free-apis

Interoperability Dimension: Structural IoP

LOST view: Technical view - application

Interoperability Saliency: The API Catalogue Data Object ABB is salient for interoperability as it is a collection of software interfaces that allows data consumption between solutions and services. 

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/APICatalogueDataObject

ABB name: eira:APICatalogueDataObject

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/APICatalogueDataObject

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

]]></skos:definition>
