	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Common Communication Network 2 (CCN 2)]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Common Communication Network 2 (CCN 2)]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: Common Communication Network 2 (CCN 2) is a pan-European telecommunications network that provides a secure and reliable platform for the exchange of information between the European Commission, EU Member States, and other participating parties.

Additional information: CCN 2 is a high-speed network that supports the exchange of information for various applications and services related to the European Union's policies and activities. It is a key component of the EU's digital infrastructure, enabling the secure and efficient transmission of data across borders. The network is managed by the European Commission's Directorate-General for Taxation and Customs Union (DG TAXUD). It is used for a wide range of applications, including customs, taxation, and agricultural policy, among others. The network is designed to ensure the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the data it transmits, using advanced security measures and protocols.

Example: Examples of applications that use the CCN 2 network include the New Computerised Transit System (NCTS), which manages the movement of goods across EU borders, and the Excise Movement and Control System (EMCS), which monitors the movement of excise goods within the EU. Another example is the Integrated Administration and Control System (IACS), which supports the management of agricultural subsidies.

Publisher: Register of the Data Protection Officer (DPO)

Source: https://ec.europa.eu/dpo-register/detail/DPR-EC-01106.1

LOST view: TVI-Wide Area Networking [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork

Name: Common Communication Network 2 (CCN 2) Communication Network

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalInfrastructure

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SecurePublicCommunicationNetwork

]]></skos:definition>
		<egovera:CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork_Properties />
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork_Properties">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Properties of Common Communication Network 2 (CCN 2)]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork_Properties</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Properties of Common Communication Network 2 (CCN 2)]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork" />
		<eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork</eira:PURI>
		<dcterms:modified>2024-01-28</dcterms:modified>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetwork2CommunicationNetwork</dcterms:identifier>
		<dcterms:title><![CDATA[Common Communication Network 2 (CCN 2) Communication Network]]></dcterms:title>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[Examples of applications that use the CCN 2 network include the New Computerised Transit System (NCTS), which manages the movement of goods across EU borders, and the Excise Movement and Control System (EMCS), which monitors the movement of excise goods within the EU. Another example is the Integrated Administration and Control System (IACS), which supports the management of agricultural subsidies.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[CCN 2 is a high-speed network that supports the exchange of information for various applications and services related to the European Union's policies and activities. It is a key component of the EU's digital infrastructure, enabling the secure and efficient transmission of data across borders. The network is managed by the European Commission's Directorate-General for Taxation and Customs Union (DG TAXUD). It is used for a wide range of applications, including customs, taxation, and agricultural policy, among others. The network is designed to ensure the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of the data it transmits, using advanced security measures and protocols.]]></skos:note>
		<dcterms:description>Common Communication Network 2 (CCN 2) is a pan-European telecommunications network that provides a secure and reliable platform for the exchange of information between the European Commission, EU Member States, and other participating parties.</dcterms:description>
		<dcterms:publisher><![CDATA[Register of the Data Protection Officer (DPO)]]></dcterms:publisher>
		<dcterms:source><![CDATA[https://ec.europa.eu/dpo-register/detail/DPR-EC-01106.1]]></dcterms:source>
		<eira:view>TVI-Wide Area Networking [Motivation]</eira:view>
		<eira:concept>eira:SolutionBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:eifLayer>TechnicalInfrastructure</eira:eifLayer>
		<eira:implementedBy>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SecurePublicCommunicationNetwork</eira:implementedBy>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetworkCommunicationNetwork">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Common Communication Network (CCN)]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetworkCommunicationNetwork</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Common Communication Network (CCN)]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: Common Communication Network (CCN) is a standardized system for transmitting and receiving data between different systems or devices. It is often used in industries such as telecommunications, computing, and networking to facilitate seamless communication and data exchange.

Additional information: CCN is a critical component in modern digital communication, enabling different systems and devices to communicate effectively. It provides a common platform for data transmission, ensuring that all systems can understand and interpret the data being sent. CCN can be used in various settings, including local area networks (LANs), wide area networks (WANs), and even the internet. It is designed to handle different types of data, including text, images, audio, and video, making it a versatile solution for many different applications.

Example: Examples of CCN application include its use in telecommunications where it allows for seamless data transmission between different devices, such as phones, computers, and servers. In computing, it can be used to facilitate communication between different systems, such as in a cloud computing environment where data needs to be shared between different servers. In networking, it can be used to connect different networks, allowing them to communicate and share data.

Publisher: Register of the Data Protection Officer (DPO)

Source: https://ec.europa.eu/dpo-register/detail/DPR-EC-04049.1

LOST view: TVI-Wide Area Networking [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetworkCommunicationNetwork

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/CommonCommunicationNetworkCommunicationNetwork

Name: Common Communication Network (CCN) Communication Network

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalInfrastructure

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/SecurePublicCommunicationNetwork

]]></skos:definition>
		<egovera:CommonCommunicationNetworkCommunicationNetwork_Properties />
	</skos:Concept>
