		<eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
		<skos:definition><![CDATA[Private Cloud Computing Facility ABB is a Facility that enables a cloud infrastructure that is exclusively dedicated to a single organization or user.]]></skos:definition>
		<eira:definitionSource><![CDATA[Inspired in Redhat]]></eira:definitionSource>
		<eira:definitionSourceReference><![CDATA[https://www.redhat.com/en/topics/cloud-computing/public-cloud-vs-private-cloud-and-hybrid-cloud]]></eira:definitionSourceReference>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): JRC- Development of the EU Green Public Procurement (GPP)- Critaria for Data Centres, Server Rooms and Cloud Services. https://ec.europa.eu/environment/gpp/pdf/jrc118558_2020_0605_data_centres_technical_report_jrc_clean_with_id.pdf]]></skos:example>
		<eira:iopSaliency><![CDATA[Private Cloud Facilities ABB is salient for organizational and technical interoperability because it establishes the business rules and responsibilities to expose public digital services that are restricted for the use of custom organizations, users or devices.]]></eira:iopSaliency>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[]]></skos:note>
