		<skos:note><![CDATA[Observability is a non-functional requirement that refers to the ability of a system to be monitored and analyzed in order to detect and diagnose issues. According to the TOGAF specification, observability is a key aspect of system performance and reliability, as it allows for proactive identification and resolution of problems before they impact users.

