		<skos:note><![CDATA[According to the TOGAF specification, Compatibility is an IT non-functional requirement that refers to the ability of a system or application to operate in conjunction with other systems or applications. This requirement ensures that the system or application can integrate seamlessly with other systems or applications without causing any disruption or compatibility issues.

Compatibility can be achieved through adherence to industry standards, protocols, and interfaces. The system or application must be designed to work with different operating systems, hardware, and software configurations. It should also be able to communicate with other systems or applications using standard communication protocols.

