		<skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage" />
		<eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage</eira:PURI>
		<dcterms:type>eira:DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage</dcterms:type>
		<dcterms:modified>2024-01-28</dcterms:modified>
		<eira:synonym></eira:synonym>
		<skos:definition><![CDATA[Digitaliation Roadmap ABB is a Work Package that corresponds to a high-level vision and strategy referring to long-term business goal an organization wants to achieve, including digital initiatives and goals the organization will drive.]]></skos:definition>
		<eira:definitionSource><![CDATA[Inspired in referent consultancy companies and IEEE]]></eira:definitionSource>
		<eira:definitionSourceReference><![CDATA[https://roadmaps.ieee.org/guide-to-technology-roadmaps]]></eira:definitionSourceReference>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[The following implementation is an example of how this specific Architecture Building Block (ABB) can be instantiated as a Solution Building Block (SBB): Digital roadmap for organising mobility authorities (OMAs). (https://cerre.eu/publications/mobility-as-a-service-maas-digital-roadmap-public-transport-authorities/)]]></skos:example>
		<eira:iopSaliency><![CDATA[Digitalization Roadmap ABB is salient for the governance, semantic and technical interoperability because it commonly offers (i) a transversal vision of existing reusable standards applied in the digitalization of the public sector, (ii) actions to ensure data exchange between digital services; (iii) technological software and assets that should be included in the digitalization of public administrations.]]></eira:iopSaliency>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:iopDimension>Governance IoP</eira:iopDimension>
		<eira:view>Organisational view</eira:view>
		<eira:viewpoint>Interoperability Governance viewpoint</eira:viewpoint>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalisationRoadmapWorkPackage</dcterms:identifier>
		<eira:eifLayer>Organisational</eira:eifLayer>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOntologiesCatalogueSolutionsGrouping">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOntologiesCatalogueSolutionsGrouping</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions (ABB) is a grouping that covers a range of ontology resources and tools that are applicable across various business domains. The catalogue includes Linked Open Vocabularies (LOV) and Ontology Design Patterns (ODP), both of which are instrumental in ontology engineering and semantic web portal design respectively.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions (ABB) is a comprehensive collection of ontology resources that are not specific to any business domain, hence the term 'agnostic'. It includes Linked Open Vocabularies (LOV), a tool used by Ontology Engineers for creating, managing and utilizing ontologies. LOV provides a wide range of vocabularies that can be linked and utilized in various contexts. Another key component of the catalogue is OntologyDesignPatterns.org (ODP), a dedicated portal for ontology design patterns. ODP provides resources and tools for designing and implementing ontologies in a semantic web context. Both LOV and ODP are crucial for ontology engineering and semantic web design, making the catalogue a valuable resource for businesses operating in diverse domains.

Example: For instance, a healthcare organization can use the LOV tool from the Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions to create a medical ontology linking various medical terms and concepts. Similarly, an e-commerce business can use the ODP resources to design a product ontology for their semantic web portal, linking various product categories and attributes.

LOST view: SV-Agnostic Ontology Catalogue

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOntologiesCatalogueSolutionsGrouping

ABB name: egovera:BusinessAgnosticOntologiesCatalogueSolutionsGrouping

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-11-20

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOntologiesCatalogueSolutionsGrouping

Name: Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions Catalogue

Interoperability Layer: Semantic

]]></skos:definition>
