Role-Based Access Control
This might involve a decision to implement role-based access control, to ensure that users only have access to the data and functions that they need for their role.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[The catalogue includes elements such as 'Authentication Mechanism', 'Encryption Standards', 'Secure Communications', 'Role-Based Access Control', 'Security Testing', 'Security Incident Response', 'Access Control Policy', 'Continuous Security Monitoring', 'Retention and Data Deletion', 'Security Incident Response Plan', 'Compliance Monitoring and Auditing', and 'Data Protection Measures'. Each of these elements represents a specific decision made in the architectural design process, with a focus on ensuring the security, privacy, and compliance of the digital solution. The decisions made in these areas can have significant impacts on the overall security posture of the solution, and as such, they are carefully documented and monitored.]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:view>Digital Solution Architecture Decisions Catalogue view</eira:view>
		<eira:eifLayer>N/A</eira:eifLayer>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticAPITechnicalInteroperabilityAgreementSolutionsGrouping">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticAPITechnicalInteroperabilityAgreementSolutionsGrouping</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions (ABB) is a grouping that refers to actual solutions that facilitate the design, development, documentation, and consumption of APIs (Application Programming Interfaces) across different systems and platforms. These solutions are built upon various specifications and protocols such as OpenAPI, RESTful API, GraphQL, gRPC, JSON-RPC, SOAP, and OData, which provide a standard, language-agnostic interface for APIs, enabling interoperability between different systems.

Additional information: The Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions (ABB) is a comprehensive suite of solutions that leverage various API specifications and protocols to ensure seamless interaction between different systems and platforms. These solutions are built upon OpenAPI, RESTful API, GraphQL, gRPC, JSON-RPC, SOAP, and OData specifications, each offering unique features and capabilities. OpenAPI is used for designing, building, documenting, and consuming REST APIs. RESTful API is a set of rules for building web services, while GraphQL is a data query and manipulation language for APIs. gRPC is a high-performance framework for service communication, JSON-RPC is a protocol for data exchange, SOAP is a messaging protocol for program communication over the internet, and OData is a protocol for building and consuming RESTful APIs.

Example: Examples of application for the Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions include designing and building APIs for a multi-language system using OpenAPI and gRPC, creating web services using RESTful API, querying and manipulating data using GraphQL, exchanging data between a client and a server using JSON-RPC, communicating between programs running on different operating systems using SOAP, and building and consuming RESTful APIs using OData.

Publisher: EIRA Team Research

LOST view: TV-Technical Agreements

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticAPITechnicalInteroperabilityAgreementSolutionsGrouping

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticAPITechnicalInteroperabilityAgreementSolutionsGrouping

Name: Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions Catalogue

Interoperability Layer: Technical

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/TechnicalInteroperabilityAgreementContract

]]></skos:definition>
