		<eira:definitionSourceReference><![CDATA[]]></eira:definitionSourceReference>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[For example, a healthcare application would need to meet the requirements of confidentiality to protect patient data, integrity to ensure the accuracy of medical records, nonrepudiation to provide proof of medical orders, accountability to track user activities, authenticity to verify the genuineness of data, auditability to provide a record of transactions, authentication to verify user identities, authorization to grant appropriate access levels, legality to comply with healthcare regulations, compliance to adhere to data protection standards, and privacy to safeguard patient privacy.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[The Security Requirements Catalogue ABB is a comprehensive collection of IT security requirements that are essential for any system or application that handles sensitive data. These requirements are designed to protect the data from unauthorized access, ensure its accuracy and consistency, provide proof of transactions, track user activities, verify user identities, grant appropriate access levels, comply with legal and regulatory standards, and safeguard privacy. Failure to meet these requirements can result in security breaches, loss of data integrity, legal penalties, and loss of trust among users and stakeholders.]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:view>Digital Solution Non-Functional Requirements Catalogue view</eira:view>
		<eira:eifLayer>N/A</eira:eifLayer>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOrganisationalGovernanceFrameworksCatalogueGrouping">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Organisational Governance Frameworks Catalogue]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOrganisationalGovernanceFrameworksCatalogueGrouping</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Organisational Governance Frameworks Catalogue]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: Organisational Governance Frameworks Catalogue ABB is a grouping that covers a set of business objects that enable the protection, confidentiality, and interoperability of data, information, and knowledge assets and the organizational resources handling them. It includes the Security Framework, Privacy Framework, and Interoperability Framework.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Organisational Governance Frameworks Catalogue ABB is a comprehensive collection of frameworks that are designed to guide organizations in managing and protecting their data and information assets. The Security Framework focuses on the protection of these assets and the resources handling them. The Privacy Framework, on the other hand, emphasizes the confidentiality aspects of these assets and resources. Lastly, the Interoperability Framework is designed to enable organizations to collaborate effectively towards the joint delivery of public services. It does this by specifying a set of common elements such as vocabulary, concepts, principles, guidelines, and recommendations.

Example: An example of the application of the Organisational Governance Frameworks Catalogue ABB could be a public service organization that needs to ensure the security and privacy of its data while also needing to collaborate with other organizations. The Security Framework would guide the organization in protecting its data and resources. The Privacy Framework would help ensure the confidentiality of the data. The Interoperability Framework would provide the necessary guidelines and recommendations for effective collaboration with other organizations.

LOST view: OV-Governance Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOrganisationalGovernanceFrameworksCatalogueGrouping

