	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticIdentityManagementSolutionsGrouping">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Identity Management Solutions]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticIdentityManagementSolutionsGrouping</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Identity Management Solutions]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Description: Bussiness Agnostic Identity Management Solutions (BAIMS) is a grouping that refers to actual solutions that facilitate the management of user identities across various business models and industries. These solutions are designed to be flexible and adaptable, allowing businesses of any type or size to effectively manage user access, authentication, and security.

Additional information: BAIMS are crucial in today's digital age where security and privacy are of utmost importance. They provide a comprehensive approach to managing the identities of users in an organization, regardless of the nature of the business. They are designed to handle tasks such as user authentication, authorization, roles and access management, password management, policy enforcement, and audit and reporting. These solutions are not tied to a specific business model or industry, making them versatile and adaptable. They can be integrated with various systems and platforms, providing a seamless user experience while ensuring security and compliance.

Example: Examples of application of BAIMS include: 1) In a healthcare setting, these solutions can be used to manage the identities of doctors, nurses, and patients, ensuring that only authorized individuals have access to sensitive patient data. 2) In a retail business, they can be used to manage the identities of customers and employees, facilitating secure transactions and protecting customer information. 3) In a financial institution, they can be used to manage the identities of account holders and employees, ensuring secure access to financial data and systems.

Publisher: EIRA Team Research

LOST view: TVA-Identification and Access Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticIdentityManagementSolutionsGrouping

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2024-01-28

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticIdentityManagementSolutionsGrouping

Name: Bussiness Agnostic Identity Management SolutionsGrouping

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Realises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalSolutionApplicationService

]]></skos:definition>
