Name: Software Architect Data Spaces Concerns Catalogue

]]></skos:definition>
		<skos:broader rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SoftwareArchitectConcernsGrouping" />
		<egovera:SoftwareArchitectDataSpacesConcernsGrouping_Properties />
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SoftwareArchitectDataSpacesConcernsGrouping_Properties">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Properties of Software Architect Data Spaces Concerns]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SoftwareArchitectDataSpacesConcernsGrouping_Properties</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Properties of Software Architect Data Spaces Concerns]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SoftwareArchitectDataSpacesConcernsGrouping" />
		<eira:PURI>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SoftwareArchitectDataSpacesConcernsGrouping</eira:PURI>
		<dcterms:modified>2023-11-19</dcterms:modified>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/SoftwareArchitectDataSpacesConcernsGrouping</dcterms:identifier>
		<dcterms:title><![CDATA[Software Architect Data Spaces Concerns Catalogue]]></dcterms:title>
		<dcterms:type>egovera:SoftwareArchitectDataSpacesConcernsGrouping</dcterms:type>
		<skos:definition><![CDATA[Software Architect Data Spaces Concerns ABB is a Grouping that covers the processes, roles, and relationships a software architect should follow to read, assess, and understand an eGovERA model for the purpose of understanding and developing a Data Spaces solution or architecture. It includes elements such as 'Technical view - application' and 'Semantic view'.]]></skos:definition>
		<eira:definitionSource><![CDATA[EIRA Team Research]]></eira:definitionSource>
		<eira:definitionSourceReference><![CDATA[]]></eira:definitionSourceReference>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[For example, a software architect might need to understand the technical infrastructure of the application, such as the programming languages used, the database management systems in place, and the server architecture.
For instance, the software architect might need to understand the semantics of the data, such as the meaning of different data fields, the relationships between different data entities, and the rules and constraints that govern the data.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[The Software Architect Data Spaces Concerns ABB is a comprehensive catalogue of elements that a software architect needs to consider when working with an eGovERA model to develop a Data Spaces solution or architecture. It includes the 'Technical view - application', which refers to the technical aspects of the application, and the 'Semantic view', which refers to the meaning and interpretation of the data. These elements are crucial in understanding the model and developing an effective solution.]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:None</eira:concept>
		<eira:view>[A] How to read the model</eira:view>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticDataMappingSolutionsGrouping">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Data Mapping Solutions]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticDataMappingSolutionsGrouping</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Data Mapping Solutions]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: Business Agnostic Data Mapping Solutions (BADS) is a grouping that covers a range of solutions designed to facilitate the mapping of data from various heterogeneous data structures and serializations to the RDF data model. These solutions are not specific to any particular business or industry, making them versatile and adaptable across different contexts. The key element in this grouping is the RDF Mapping Language (RML), a generic mapping language that extends the W3C-standardized mapping language, R2RML.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Business Agnostic Data Mapping Solutions catalogue primarily includes the RDF Mapping Language (RML), a mapping language that allows for the expression of customized mapping rules from various data structures and serializations to the RDF data model. RML is a superset of R2RML, the W3C standard for expressing customized mappings from relational databases to RDF. As such, RML follows the same syntax as R2RML and extends its applicability and scope by adding support for data in other structured formats. RML mappings are themselves RDF graphs, and this document provides a comprehensive description of the RML language and its concepts through definitions and examples.

Example: An example of the application of Business Agnostic Data Mapping Solutions would be in a scenario where a business needs to map data from a relational database to RDF. Using RML, the business can express customized mapping rules to convert the data from the relational database into the RDF data model. This allows for greater interoperability and flexibility in data management and usage.

LOST view: SV-Data Mapping

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticDataMappingSolutionsGrouping

ABB name: egovera:BusinessAgnosticDataMappingSolutionsGrouping

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-11-20

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticDataMappingSolutionsGrouping

Name: Business Agnostic Data Mapping Solutions Catalogue

Interoperability Layer: Semantic

]]></skos:definition>
		<skos:related rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/RDFMappingLanguageDataObject" />
