		<skos:example><![CDATA[An example of the application of the Legislation on Behavioural Interoperability (NBI) is in the healthcare sector. Here, different systems such as electronic health records, hospital information systems, and telemedicine applications need to interact seamlessly to provide effective and efficient healthcare services. The NBI legislation ensures that these systems can exchange information and services in a predictable and consistent manner, promoting interoperability and integration.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[The Legislation on Behavioural Interoperability (NBI) is an important aspect of information technology and telecommunications. It is concerned with the ability of different systems, applications, and services to work together seamlessly. This involves not only the technical aspects of interoperability but also the legal and regulatory aspects. The NBI legislation provides a framework for ensuring that systems behave in a predictable and consistent manner when they interact, facilitating the exchange of information and services. It covers a wide range of areas, including data exchange standards, communication protocols, interface specifications, and service level agreements.]]></skos:note>
