		<skos:definition><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Business Information Base (ABB) is a grouping that refers to the actual catalogue of information entities that covers a wide range of business-related elements. These elements include payments, transactions, identification, qualifications, audit trails, access rights, profiles, messages, availability, digital signatures, documents, security measures, locations, invoices, contracting authorities, economic operators, digital assets, credentials, data quality, and distribution lists.]]></skos:definition>
		<eira:definitionSource><![CDATA[EIRA Team Research]]></eira:definitionSource>
