		<eira:definitionSourceReference><![CDATA[]]></eira:definitionSourceReference>
		<skos:example><![CDATA[An example of the application of the Legislation on Structural Interoperability (EBI) ABB is the use of electronic signatures in cross-border transactions within the EU. Under Regulation 2014910 (eIDAS), these signatures are legally valid and recognized across member states, facilitating electronic transactions and promoting the digital single market. Another example is the sharing of information on cyber threats and incidents between member states under Regulation 2018389, which enhances EU cybersecurity capabilities and strengthens the resilience of its digital infrastructure.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[The Legislation on Structural Interoperability (EBI) ABB includes two key regulations. The first, Regulation 2014910, also known as eIDAS, provides a legal framework for electronic signatures, seals, time stamps, documents, and registered delivery services, ensuring their legal validity and cross-border recognition within the EU. The second, Regulation 2018389, establishes a framework for cooperation and information exchange in the field of cybersecurity, setting out rules for sharing information on cyber threats and incidents, coordinating response measures, and establishing a European Cybersecurity Certification Framework.]]></skos:note>
		<eira:concept>eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock</eira:concept>
		<eira:view>LV-Architecture Principles</eira:view>
		<eira:view>LV-Binding Power and Jurisdiction</eira:view>
		<eira:eifLayer>Legal</eira:eifLayer>
	</skos:Concept>
	<skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOrganisationalAgreementSolutionsGrouping">
		<skos:notation><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Organisational Agreement Solutions]]></skos:notation>
		<dcterms:identifier>http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOrganisationalAgreementSolutionsGrouping</dcterms:identifier>
		<skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Business Agnostic Organisational Agreement Solutions]]></skos:prefLabel>
		<skos:topConceptOf rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8" />
		<skos:definition xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[Definition: Business Agnostic Organisational Agreement Solutions (BAOAS) is a grouping that refers to the actual catalogue of specifications, agreements and/or contracts that facilitates the establishment of standardised business practices across various industries. This catalogue includes a variety of elements, such as codes of conduct, guidelines, and best practices, which are designed to improve operational efficiency, promote ethical business practices, and enhance environmental sustainability.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The elements contained within the BAOAS catalogue are diverse and cater to different aspects of business operations. For instance, it includes the 'Code of Conduct for Energy Efficiency in Data Centres', a voluntary code developed by the European Commission's Joint Research Centre. This code aims to improve the energy efficiency and environmental sustainability of data centres by providing guidelines and best practices for data centre operators to reduce their environmental impact. The BAOAS catalogue is designed to be business agnostic, meaning it can be applied across various industries and business models. It serves as a valuable resource for organisations seeking to adopt standardised, ethical, and sustainable business practices.

Example: An example of the application of BAOAS could be a data centre operator utilising the 'Code of Conduct for Energy Efficiency in Data Centres' to improve their energy efficiency. They could implement the guidelines and best practices outlined in the code, such as optimising cooling systems or using energy-efficient hardware, to reduce their environmental impact. Similarly, a company in a different industry could use other elements within the BAOAS catalogue to standardise their business practices and enhance their operational efficiency.

LOST view: Organisational view

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOrganisationalAgreementSolutionsGrouping

