		<dcterms:title><![CDATA[Scalability Requirements Catalogue Catalogue]]></dcterms:title>
		<dcterms:type>eira:ScalabilityRequirementsCatalogueGrouping</dcterms:type>
		<skos:definition><![CDATA[Scalability Requirements Catalogue ABB is a grouping that covers a range of non-functional IT requirements that are critical for ensuring the scalability, performance, and efficiency of a system or application. It includes elements such as Traffic Pattern, Elasticity, and Latency, each of which plays a key role in determining how well a system can handle user traffic and respond to changes in demand.]]></skos:definition>
