		<skos:example><![CDATA[An example of Containerization Enablers ABB in action is the use of Docker as a container platform to package an application and its dependencies into a single object, and Kubernetes as a container orchestrator to manage the deployment and scaling of the Docker containers across a cluster of servers in a cloud environment. This allows for efficient, reliable, and scalable deployment of applications.]]></skos:example>
		<skos:note><![CDATA[Containerization Enablers ABB is a crucial component in modern software development and deployment processes. It includes the '[Container]' and '[Containers Orchestrator]' elements. The '[Container]' is a lightweight and portable software package that includes everything needed to run an application, ensuring a consistent and isolated environment for applications to run across different computing environments. The '[Containers Orchestrator]' is a software tool or platform that automates the deployment, management, and scaling of containerized applications, providing a centralized control plane to efficiently manage and coordinate the deployment and operation of containers across a cluster of machines or nodes.]]></skos:note>
